From 22d18b643bdafefefd41a0c81c18affe7b3820c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:25:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Pass a Ctrl-C that came before the job took the terminal on
 to the job

On Redox the time between the end of the line and the job taking the
terminal is long enough to type Ctrl-C into. The SIGINT then reaches the
shell, which only notes it; the job runs to its end, and the shell
reports "process (<shell pid>) ended by signal SIGINT" afterwards.

The shell now forgets signals noted before the line was read, and passes
a SIGINT noted since then on to the foreground job when it starts
watching it. (redox-rpi #86)
